description:
Design a circuit that implements a light control system using multiple sensors. The module reads digital values from a specified number of light sensors and averages their outputs to determine the ambient light level. Based on this calculated ambient light, it adjusts the brightness level through a dimming control mechanism, which provides outputs of varying intensities: maximum, 75%, 50%, and 25% brightness depending on the ambient light range. The output signals a dimming level that corresponds to the light conditions detected by the sensors.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] sensor,
  input clk, // Added clk input
  output reg dimming // Changed output to reg type
);

testbench:
