description:
Design a debounce circuit for a bouncy input signal. The module uses a clock signal to sample the bouncy input and employs a counter to filter out noise during a predefined time period. The output, debounced, indicates a stable signal when the input remains consistent across three clock cycles. The design effectively addresses signal integrity issues by ensuring that transient fluctuations in the input do not affect the output, thus providing a reliable signal for subsequent logic processing.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input bouncy,
  output debounced
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input bouncy,
  output debounced
);reg [18:0] counter;
reg d1, d2, d3;
assign debounced = d1 & d2 & d3;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (&counter) begin
    counter <= 0;
    d1 <= bouncy;
    d2 <= d1;
    d3 <= d2;
  end else
    counter <= counter + 1'b1;
end

endmodule

