description:
Develop a pulse width modulation (PWM) generator that outputs a PWM signal based on an 8-bit duty cycle input. The module uses a clock signal to increment a counter, and it adjusts the output based on a calculated threshold derived from the duty cycle. The output, `pwm_out`, is set high for a portion of the clock cycle determined by the duty cycle percentage, effectively allowing control over the signal's average power delivered to a load. The PWM frequency is defined by the clock and the resolution of the counter, which in this case is set to an 8-bit value.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] duty_cycle,
  output reg pwm_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] duty_cycle,
  output reg pwm_out
);parameter resolution = 8; // resolution of the PWM signal

reg [resolution-1:0] counter;
reg [7:0] threshold;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter >= resolution) begin
    counter <= 0;
  end
  if (duty_cycle > 100) begin
    threshold <= resolution;
  end else begin
    threshold <= (duty_cycle * resolution) / 100;
  end
  if (counter < threshold) begin
    pwm_out <= 1;
  end else begin
    pwm_out <= 0;
  end
end

endmodule

