description:
Design a synchronous input circuit that debounces a button signal. On the rising edge of the clock, it captures the current state of the button, storing it in two registers to filter out noise from mechanical bouncing. The output `syncBtn` is set to HIGH when the button transitions from LOW to HIGH and is set to LOW when the button transitions from HIGH to LOW, providing a clean, synchronized signal for further processing.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input btn,
  output reg syncBtn = 0
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input btn,
  output reg syncBtn = 0
);reg b1;
    reg b2;
    always @(posedge clk) begin
      b1 <= btn;
      b2 <= b1;
      if (b1 && !b2) begin
        syncBtn <= 1;
      end
      if (!b1 && b2) begin
        syncBtn <= 0;
      end
    end
endmodule

