description:
Design a control logic module that generates a single output signal, `mode_SSHRin`, based on a 4-bit input `rd_stage` and a clock signal. The output is reset to LOW when the `rst` signal is active. On each positive edge of the clock, `mode_SSHRin` is set HIGH if both the second and zeroth bits of `rd_stage` are HIGH, or if both the third and first bits are HIGH. This module is intended to manage operational modes in a digital circuit by determining a specific condition from the current state indicated by `rd_stage`.
module top_module(
         rd_stage,mode_SSHRin,rst,clk);

code:
module top_module(
         rd_stage,mode_SSHRin,rst,clk);input[3:0] rd_stage;
  output reg mode_SSHRin;
  input rst,clk;





  always @(posedge clk)
  begin
    if (rst) mode_SSHRin = 1'b0;
    else mode_SSHRin = &{rd_stage[2],rd_stage[0]} || &{rd_stage[3],rd_stage[1]};
  end 
endmodule

