description:
Design a synchronous state machine that transitions through three states: IDLE, COUNT, and DONE. Upon reset, the machine initializes in the IDLE state. In IDLE, it transitions to the COUNT state, where it starts counting up sequentially. Once it reaches a certain condition (count state interpreted as 2'b11), it transitions to the DONE state. From DONE, it resets back to IDLE. This design is suitable for applications that require a controlled counting sequence and state management with reset capability.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input reset,
  output reg [1:0] state
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input reset,
  output reg [1:0] state
);parameter IDLE = 2'b00;
  parameter COUNT = 2'b01;
  parameter DONE = 2'b10;

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (reset) begin
      state <= IDLE;
    end else begin
      case (state)
        IDLE: begin
          state <= COUNT;
        end
        COUNT: begin
          if (state == 2'b11) begin
            state <= DONE;
          end else begin
            state <= state + 1;
          end
        end
        DONE: begin
          state <= IDLE;
        end
      endcase
    end
  end

endmodule

