Design a forwarding unit that determines data forwarding conditions in a pipelined processor architecture. It generates two control signals, `forward_a` and `forward_b`, based on whether the write-back stage is writing back to the registers identified by `rs_id` and `rt_id`. If the write-back address matches either input register and a write operation is occurring (indicated by `reg_write_mem`), the respective forward signal is asserted to enable forwarding of data from the memory stage to the execution stage, thereby preventing hazards in instruction execution.
