Design a glitch filter circuit that uses a shift register technique to stabilize an input signal. The module samples the input `in` on every positive clock edge and stores it across a series of delay elements for `delay_cycles` clock cycles. The output `out` is then taken from the last element in the delay chain, effectively filtering out short glitches on the `in` signal by requiring it to be stable for a specified duration before it appears at the output.
